From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gts2-common: build the OMX resource manager from source

The Exynos OMX core loads its components from /vendor/lib/omx/, and every
component then asks libExynosOMX_Resourcemanager for a decoder slot. The
resource manager blob of gts2-common reads the component's codecType at
offset 0x18 of the base component and accepts only 1..5; the component
blobs (libOMX.Exynos.AVC.Decoder.so, ...MPEG4.Decoder.so) store it at
0x1c. The blobs are from different BSP generations, so every node failed
with "Exynos_OMX_Get_Resource()" / InsufficientResources and no hardware
decoder was available.

The resource manager built from hardware/samsung_slsi/openmax reads 0x1c,
has the same soname and NEEDED set and exports every symbol the
components import (the blob's three extra exports, DataSpaceToColorSpace,
Mmap and Munmap, are imported by nothing). Leave the blob out of
PRODUCT_COPY_FILES so the source-built module (LOCAL_PROPRIETARY_MODULE)
is installed in its place. The OMX core stays the blob.

Tested on the SM-T815 on 2026-11-08 by swapping the library on the
device: OMX.Exynos.avc.dec, .avc.dec.secure and mpeg4.dec allocate;
1080p AVC decodes at about 15 ms per frame against 55 ms in software;
the secure decoder configures and starts with a Widevine L1 MediaCrypto
("DRM instance is opened"). Logs: logs/omx-test2-20261108/.
---
diff --git a/gts2-common/gts2-common-vendor.mk b/gts2-common/gts2-common-vendor.mk
index b0e20bb..e268787 100644
--- a/gts2-common/gts2-common-vendor.mk
+++ b/gts2-common/gts2-common-vendor.mk
@@ -19,4 +19,8 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += libGLES_mali
 include vendor/samsung/gts2-common/find-vendor-blobs.mk
 
 # Proprietary blobs
-PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += $(call find-vendor-blobs,vendor/samsung/gts2-common/proprietary)
+# libExynosOMX_Resourcemanager.so is built from hardware/samsung_slsi/openmax instead: the blob
+# reads the OMX component's codecType at offset 0x18, the Exynos OMX component blobs write it at
+# 0x1c (another BSP generation), so every component failed with InsufficientResources.
+PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += $(filter-out %/libExynosOMX_Resourcemanager.so, \
+    $(call find-vendor-blobs,vendor/samsung/gts2-common/proprietary))
